# rpg/art/doll/clips/actions/staff.clip: the staff family on both bodies (P2c wave 2, ACTIONS-2H; STYLE_P2 12, 25.8):
# the guard (held across), hit 1 the diagonal two-handed strike (drawn back across the body over the shoulder, the
# diagonal at full reach, swinging through), hit 2 the rising strike, hit 3 the overhead smash (the finisher: the
# staff overhead, the smash level at the ground line, the bounce), the block (the haft up across), the drawn walk / run.
# A fighter's staff (`when staff`); the walking stick and a civil staff keep the generic clips. Timing at pace 1.0.
# (wave-2 fix round, ACTIONS r1: B12 BOOT on m11_staff drun L5) the drawn run facing L leans a step further at each
# bound (frames 2 and 5, the flight: lean -5), which carries the staff a pixel forward so its butt clears the far boot
# (it left a 1 px sliver of it). The angles stay a045 / a135: D81 asks both fists on the haft line in a drawn frame.
# (PLAN D81: no weapon pixel more than 2 rows below the sole row) hit 2 coils twice on st_2a (frame 2 keeps frame 1's
# arms and angle, a202 / a337, and crouches a row deeper): st_2b's low coil hung the staff 8-10 rows under the soles
# and no angle on st_2b holds both fists on the haft above the ground; hit 1's follow facing L keeps a225 standing a
# row taller (no bob), its staff 3 rows under the soles before.
# (wave-2 fix round 4, ACTIONS; C3d) hit 3's follow facing U on the hit-2 follow arms (st_2f): st_3f's fist sat under a
# cape's edge with one pixel showing, the grip under the cape (2 lines).

